Read a backwards number range in a script the right way round.

CAVE2/WR207.MOV (the water in scene C2_18) tests Jack's motion against
"1 or 66..64", which never matches 64 to 66, and the engine printed
"testExpr cmp 66,64" for it on every frame. The same rule in the 19
other water scripts reads "1 or 64..66". Swap the bounds instead of
warning; no other script in the game has a backwards range.

--- a/opcodes.cpp
+++ b/opcodes.cpp
@@ -135,7 +135,8 @@
 			int16_t cmp1 = _objectScript.fetchNextWord();
 			int16_t cmp2 = _objectScript.fetchNextWord();
 			if (cmp1 > cmp2) {
-				warning("testExpr cmp %d,%d", cmp1, cmp2);
+				// CAVE2/WR207.MOV says 66..64 where the other water scripts say 64..66
+				SWAP(cmp1, cmp2);
 			}
 			if (cmp1 <= val && cmp2 >= val) {
 				ret = true;
